d=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"azq-305-practice-test-1-explanation-6" data-azq=
-explain-toggle=3D"" aria-disabled=3D"false" style=3D"display: inline-flex;=
" fdprocessedid=3D"40xorp">Hide explanation</button><div class=3D"azq-expla=
nation is-open" id=3D"azq-305-practice-test-1-explanation-6">
            <h3>The correct answers are Enterprise applications and App reg=
istrations.</h3>
            <p>Enterprise applications in Azure AD represent the SaaS or on=
-premises apps you want to integrate for SSO. App registrations provide the=
 identity configuration and credentials that allow these applications to co=
mmunicate with Azure AD for authentication. Together, they allow users to a=
ccess applications using their Azure AD credentials, enabling seamless SSO.=
 Proper configuration of these components is essential to maintain a secure=
 and integrated identity solution. SSO reduces the need for users to rememb=
er multiple passwords and enhances organizational security.</p>
