      <section aria-labelledby=3D"azq-q9-text" class=3D"azq-question" data-=
correct=3D"true" data-question=3D"9" data-type=3D"true-false" data-category=
=3D"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions">
        <div class=3D"azq-question-body">
          <p class=3D"azq-question-text" id=3D"azq-q9-text"><span class=3D"=
azq-question-number">Question 9:</span> Azure AD Conditional Access policie=
s can require MFA only for risky sign-ins.</p>
          <ul class=3D"azq-options">
            <li class=3D"azq-option"><input autocomplete=3D"off" id=3D"q9tr=
ue" name=3D"q9" type=3D"radio" value=3D"true"><label for=3D"q9true"><span>T=
rue</span></label></li>
            <li class=3D"azq-option"><input autocomplete=3D"off" id=3D"q9fa=
lse" name=3D"q9" type=3D"radio" value=3D"false"><label for=3D"q9false"><spa=
n>False</span></label></li>
          </ul>
          <button class=3D"azq-explain-toggle" type=3D"button" aria-expande=
d=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"azq-305-practice-test-1-explanation-9" data-azq=
-explain-toggle=3D"" aria-disabled=3D"false" style=3D"display: inline-flex;=
" fdprocessedid=3D"ommk0o">Hide explanation</button><div class=3D"azq-expla=
nation is-open" id=3D"azq-305-practice-test-1-explanation-9">
            <h3>The correct answer is True.</h3>
            <p>Azure AD Conditional Access policies are highly flexible and=
 can be tailored to target specific scenarios, such as requiring multi-fact=
or authentication (MFA) only for sign-ins deemed risky by Identity Protecti=
on. This helps balance security with user convenience, as users are only pr=
ompted for additional authentication when necessary. Conditional Access use=
s signals like user location, device state, and sign-in risk to enforce pol=
icies. By focusing MFA on risky sign-ins, organizations can strengthen secu=
rity while reducing unnecessary friction for trusted users. This targeted a=
pproach improves the overall user experience.</p>
            <h4>Related Microsoft Learn topic</h4>
            <p><a href=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governanc=
e/" rel=3D"noopener" target=3D"_blank">Azure governance documentation</a></=
p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
