alse" name=3D"q10" type=3D"radio" value=3D"false"><label for=3D"q10false"><=
span>False</span></label></li>
          </ul>
          <button class=3D"azq-explain-toggle" type=3D"button" aria-expande=
d=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"azq-305-practice-test-1-explanation-10" data-az=
q-explain-toggle=3D"" aria-disabled=3D"false" style=3D"display: inline-flex=
;" fdprocessedid=3D"xhling">Hide explanation</button><div class=3D"azq-expl=
anation is-open" id=3D"azq-305-practice-test-1-explanation-10">
            <h3>The correct answer is True.</h3>
            <p>Azure Policy supports not only compliance detection but also=
 automated remediation tasks, known as policy initiatives or remediation ta=
sks. For example, if a required tag is missing on a resource, Azure Policy =
can automatically apply the tag to bring the resource into compliance. Reme=
diation can also include deploying specific configurations or settings as r=
equired by policy definitions. This automation greatly reduces manual inter=
vention and supports ongoing compliance. Regular policy evaluation and reme=
diation are essential for governance at scale.</p>
            <h4>Related Microsoft Learn topic</h4>
            <p><a href=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governanc=
e/" rel=3D"noopener" target=3D"_blank">Azure governance documentation</a></=
p>
