nation is-open" id=3D"azq-305-practice-test-1-explanation-15">
            <h3>The correct answer is Azure Cosmos DB.</h3>
            <p>Cosmos DB is a globally distributed, multi-model NoSQL datab=
ase service. It is optimized for high throughput and low latency, making it=
 suitable for mission-critical applications that require fast, consistent r=
esponses. Cosmos DB supports multiple APIs, including SQL, MongoDB, Cassand=
ra, and Gremlin. It also provides comprehensive SLA-backed guarantees for p=
erformance and availability. This makes Cosmos DB a strong choice for moder=
n cloud applications needing flexible, scalable, and resilient data storage=
.</p>
