            <p>NSGs allow you to define inbound and outbound security rules=
 at the subnet or network interface level, controlling traffic flow. Applic=
ation Security Groups enable you to group VMs with similar functions and ap=
ply network rules collectively, simplifying management. Both features work =
together to enforce granular network security in Azure virtual networks. Th=
is approach enhances defense-in-depth and supports zero-trust architectures=
