          <p class=3D"azq-question-text" id=3D"azq-q46-text"><span class=3D=
"azq-question-number">Question 46:</span> Azure Firewall can filter both in=
bound and outbound network traffic.</p>
          <ul class=3D"azq-options">
            <li class=3D"azq-option"><input autocomplete=3D"off" id=3D"q46t=
rue" name=3D"q46" type=3D"radio" value=3D"true"><label for=3D"q46true"><spa=
n>True</span></label></li>
            <li class=3D"azq-option"><input autocomplete=3D"off" id=3D"q46f=
alse" name=3D"q46" type=3D"radio" value=3D"false"><label for=3D"q46false"><=
span>False</span></label></li>
          </ul>
          <button class=3D"azq-explain-toggle" type=3D"button" aria-expande=
d=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"azq-305-practice-test-1-explanation-46" data-az=
q-explain-toggle=3D"" aria-disabled=3D"false" style=3D"display: inline-flex=
;" fdprocessedid=3D"qlvyap">Hide explanation</button><div class=3D"azq-expl=
anation is-open" id=3D"azq-305-practice-test-1-explanation-46">
            <h3>The correct answer is True.</h3>
            <p>Azure Firewall is a fully stateful, managed firewall service=
 that inspects, logs, and controls both inbound and outbound traffic for yo=
ur Azure virtual networks. It supports both application and network rule co=
llections, allowing granular control over traffic flows. You can enforce po=
licies to restrict access to internet, between subnets, or even block known=
 malicious domains. Azure Firewall integrates with threat intelligence to a=
ctively block traffic from or to known bad IP addresses. Its scalability an=
d deep integration with Azure make it a central component of cloud network =
security.</p>
            <h4>Related Microsoft Learn topic</h4>
            <p><a href=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architect=
ure/" rel=3D"noopener" target=3D"_blank">Azure Architecture Center</a></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby=3D"azq-q47-text" class=3D"azq-question" data=
-correct=3D"false" data-question=3D"47" data-type=3D"true-false" data-categ=
ory=3D"Design infrastructure solutions">
        <div class=3D"azq-question-body">
          <p class=3D"azq-question-text" id=3D"azq-q47-text"><span class=3D=
"azq-question-number">Question 47:</span> Azure Application Gateway only su=
pports Layer 4 load balancing.</p>
          <ul class=3D"azq-options">
            <li class=3D"azq-option"><input autocomplete=3D"off" id=3D"q47t=
rue" name=3D"q47" type=3D"radio" value=3D"true"><label for=3D"q47true"><spa=
n>True</span></label></li>
            <li class=3D"azq-option"><input autocomplete=3D"off" id=3D"q47f=
alse" name=3D"q47" type=3D"radio" value=3D"false"><label for=3D"q47false"><=
span>False</span></label></li>
          </ul>
          <button class=3D"azq-explain-toggle" type=3D"button" aria-expande=
d=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"azq-305-practice-test-1-explanation-47" data-az=
q-explain-toggle=3D"" aria-disabled=3D"false" style=3D"display: inline-flex=
;" fdprocessedid=3D"kn5tlh">Hide explanation</button><div class=3D"azq-expl=
anation is-open" id=3D"azq-305-practice-test-1-explanation-47">
            <h3>The correct answer is False.</h3>
            <p>Azure Application Gateway is designed as a Layer 7 (applicat=
ion layer) load balancer, providing advanced routing and application delive=
ry features. Unlike traditional load balancers that work at the transport l=
ayer, Application Gateway can make routing decisions based on HTTP/S attrib=
utes such as URL path or host headers. It supports SSL termination, cookie-=
based session affinity, and a Web Application Firewall (WAF) to protect aga=
inst common threats. These capabilities are vital for modern web applicatio=
ns requiring intelligent routing and enhanced security. Using Application G=
ateway ensures optimized and secure delivery of your web workloads.</p>
            <h4>Related Microsoft Learn topic</h4>
            <p><a href=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architect=
ure/" rel=3D"noopener" target=3D"_blank">Azure Architecture Center</a></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby=3D"azq-q48-text" class=3D"azq-question" data=
-correct=3D"true" data-question=3D"48" data-type=3D"true-false" data-catego=
ry=3D"Design infrastructure solutions">
        <div class=3D"azq-question-body">
          <p class=3D"azq-question-text" id=3D"azq-q48-text"><span class=3D=
"azq-question-number">Question 48:</span> Azure Bastion allows secure RDP/S=
SH access to virtual machines without exposing public IP addresses.</p>
          <ul class=3D"azq-options">
            <li class=3D"azq-option"><input autocomplete=3D"off" id=3D"q48t=
rue" name=3D"q48" type=3D"radio" value=3D"true"><label for=3D"q48true"><spa=
n>True</span></label></li>
            <li class=3D"azq-option"><input autocomplete=3D"off" id=3D"q48f=
alse" name=3D"q48" type=3D"radio" value=3D"false"><label for=3D"q48false"><=
span>False</span></label></li>
          </ul>
          <button class=3D"azq-explain-toggle" type=3D"button" aria-expande=
d=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"azq-305-practice-test-1-explanation-48" data-az=
q-explain-toggle=3D"" aria-disabled=3D"false" style=3D"display: inline-flex=
;" fdprocessedid=3D"a4ufj">Hide explanation</button><div class=3D"azq-expla=
nation is-open" id=3D"azq-305-practice-test-1-explanation-48">
            <h3>The correct answer is True.</h3>
            <p>Azure Bastion is a fully managed service that provides seaml=
ess and secure RDP and SSH connectivity to virtual machines directly throug=
h the Azure portal. By using Bastion, you eliminate the need to assign publ=
ic IP addresses to your VMs, reducing the attack surface for brute-force at=
tacks. Traffic is tunneled over SSL, ensuring data confidentiality and inte=
grity during sessions. This service is especially valuable for organization=
s with strict security requirements or zero-trust architectures. Using Azur=
e Bastion greatly enhances your security posture for remote administration.=
</p>
            <h4>Related Microsoft Learn topic</h4>
            <p><a href=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architect=
ure/" rel=3D"noopener" target=3D"_blank">Azure Architecture Center</a></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby=3D"azq-q49-text" class=3D"azq-question" data=
-correct=3D"a" data-question=3D"49" data-type=3D"single-choice" data-catego=
ry=3D"Design infrastructure solutions">
        <div class=3D"azq-question-body">
          <p class=3D"azq-question-text" id=3D"azq-q49-text"><span class=3D=
"azq-question-number">Question 49:</span> Which feature can be used to auto=
mate configuration and deployment of resources according to predefined stan=
dards?</p>
          <ul class=3D"azq-options">
            <li class=3D"azq-option"><input autocomplete=3D"off" id=3D"q49a=
" name=3D"q49" type=3D"radio" value=3D"a"><label for=3D"q49a"><span>Azure B=
lueprints</span></label></li>
            <li class=3D"azq-option"><input autocomplete=3D"off" id=3D"q49b=
" name=3D"q49" type=3D"radio" value=3D"b"><label for=3D"q49b"><span>Azure S=
QL Database</span></label></li>
            <li class=3D"azq-option"><input autocomplete=3D"off" id=3D"q49c=
" name=3D"q49" type=3D"radio" value=3D"c"><label for=3D"q49c"><span>Azure T=
raffic Manager</span></label></li>
            <li class=3D"azq-option"><input autocomplete=3D"off" id=3D"q49d=
" name=3D"q49" type=3D"radio" value=3D"d"><label for=3D"q49d"><span>Azure K=
ey Vault</span></label></li>
          </ul>
          <button class=3D"azq-explain-toggle" type=3D"button" aria-expande=
d=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"azq-305-practice-test-1-explanation-49" data-az=
q-explain-toggle=3D"" aria-disabled=3D"false" style=3D"display: inline-flex=
;" fdprocessedid=3D"v7wrnz">Hide explanation</button><div class=3D"azq-expl=
anation is-open" id=3D"azq-305-practice-test-1-explanation-49">
            <h3>The correct answer is Azure Blueprints.</h3>
            <p>Azure Blueprints lets you orchestrate the deployment of a se=
t of resource templates, policies, and RBAC assignments as a single, repeat=
able package. This ensures that environments are created consistently and i=
n compliance with organizational or regulatory requirements. Blueprints are=
 especially useful for large enterprises or regulated industries that need =
to enforce standardized deployments across teams or projects. You can versi=
on and update blueprints as your standards evolve, enabling agile yet contr=
olled infrastructure management. Leveraging Blueprints helps minimize confi=
guration drift and speeds up environment provisioning.</p>
            <h4>Related Microsoft Learn topic</h4>
            <p><a href=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architect=
ure/" rel=3D"noopener" target=3D"_blank">Azure Architecture Center</a></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby=3D"azq-q50-text" class=3D"azq-question" data=
-correct=3D"a" data-question=3D"50" data-type=3D"single-choice" data-catego=
ry=3D"Design infrastructure solutions">
        <div class=3D"azq-question-body">
          <p class=3D"azq-question-text" id=3D"azq-q50-text"><span class=3D=
"azq-question-number">Question 50:</span> What is the primary purpose of Az=
ure Private Link?</p>
          <ul class=3D"azq-options">
            <li class=3D"azq-option"><input autocomplete=3D"off" id=3D"q50a=
" name=3D"q50" type=3D"radio" value=3D"a"><label for=3D"q50a"><span>Provide=
 private connectivity to Azure services over the Microsoft backbone</span><=
/label></li>
            <li class=3D"azq-option"><input autocomplete=3D"off" id=3D"q50b=
" name=3D"q50" type=3D"radio" value=3D"b"><label for=3D"q50b"><span>Encrypt=
 data at rest</span></label></li>
            <li class=3D"azq-option"><input autocomplete=3D"off" id=3D"q50c=
" name=3D"q50" type=3D"radio" value=3D"c"><label for=3D"q50c"><span>Create =
a global VNet</span></label></li>
            <li class=3D"azq-option"><input autocomplete=3D"off" id=3D"q50d=
" name=3D"q50" type=3D"radio" value=3D"d"><label for=3D"q50d"><span>Impleme=
nt DDoS protection</span></label></li>
          </ul>
          <button class=3D"azq-explain-toggle" type=3D"button" aria-expande=
d=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"azq-305-practice-test-1-explanation-50" data-az=
q-explain-toggle=3D"" aria-disabled=3D"false" style=3D"display: inline-flex=
;" fdprocessedid=3D"cbftnh">Hide explanation</button><div class=3D"azq-expl=
anation is-open" id=3D"azq-305-practice-test-1-explanation-50">
            <h3>The correct answer is Provide private connectivity to Azure=
 services over the Microsoft backbone.</h3>
            <p>Azure Private Link allows you to access PaaS services like A=
zure Storage or SQL Database privately from within your virtual network, by=
passing the public internet. This enhances security by preventing data exfi=
ltration risks and allows you to meet stringent compliance requirements. Pr=
ivate Link can be used with both Microsoft and third-party services availab=
le in Azure Marketplace. By using Private Link, you ensure that sensitive d=
ata remains within your organization's trusted network boundaries. It's a r=
ecommended practice for securing communications between your workloads and =
Azure services.</p>
            <h4>Related Microsoft Learn topic</h4>
            <p><a href=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architect=
ure/" rel=3D"noopener" target=3D"_blank">Azure Architecture Center</a></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby=3D"azq-q51-text" class=3D"azq-question" data=
-correct=3D"a" data-question=3D"51" data-type=3D"single-choice" data-catego=
ry=3D"Design infrastructure solutions">
        <div class=3D"azq-question-body">
          <p class=3D"azq-question-text" id=3D"azq-q51-text"><span class=3D=
"azq-question-number">Question 51:</span> Which solution is recommended for=
 hosting serverless event-driven workloads in Azure?</p>
          <ul class=3D"azq-options">
            <li class=3D"azq-option"><input autocomplete=3D"off" id=3D"q51a=
" name=3D"q51" type=3D"radio" value=3D"a"><label for=3D"q51a"><span>Azure F=
unctions</span></label></li>
            <li class=3D"azq-option"><input autocomplete=3D"off" id=3D"q51b=
" name=3D"q51" type=3D"radio" value=3D"b"><label for=3D"q51b"><span>Azure V=
M</span></label></li>
            <li class=3D"azq-option"><input autocomplete=3D"off" id=3D"q51c=
" name=3D"q51" type=3D"radio" value=3D"c"><label for=3D"q51c"><span>Azure S=
QL Database</span></label></li>
            <li class=3D"azq-option"><input autocomplete=3D"off" id=3D"q51d=
" name=3D"q51" type=3D"radio" value=3D"d"><label for=3D"q51d"><span>Azure E=
xpressRoute</span></label></li>
          </ul>
          <button class=3D"azq-explain-toggle" type=3D"button" aria-expande=
d=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"azq-305-practice-test-1-explanation-51" data-az=
q-explain-toggle=3D"" aria-disabled=3D"false" style=3D"display: inline-flex=
;" fdprocessedid=3D"x97g9h">Hide explanation</button><div class=3D"azq-expl=
anation is-open" id=3D"azq-305-practice-test-1-explanation-51">
            <h3>The correct answer is Azure Functions.</h3>
            <p>Azure Functions is a serverless compute service that lets yo=
u run code in response to events or triggers without having to manage serve=
rs. It automatically scales to handle varying workloads, charging you only =
for actual usage, not pre-provisioned resources. Functions are ideal for bu=
ilding microservices, automating tasks, or integrating with other Azure and=
 external services through bindings and triggers. This approach reduces ope=
rational overhead and accelerates time to market for new features. Serverle=
ss architectures like Azure Functions are increasingly popular for agile, e=
vent-driven cloud applications.</p>
            <h4>Related Microsoft Learn topic</h4>
            <p><a href=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architect=
ure/" rel=3D"noopener" target=3D"_blank">Azure Architecture Center</a></p>
